 ## Overview
-This method offloads the computationally intensive geometry operations of volume rendering—specifically perspective calculations, gradient estimation, and volume data resampling—to dedicated hardware accelerators. It solves the bottleneck where software implementations consume up to 80% of computation time on these tasks [S1]. Unlike general-purpose GPU implementations that rely on texture sampling hardware, this method uses custom address generation and precalculated weight memories to perform backward mapping interpolation and gradient estimation in parallel, generating ray starting points and sample values for downstream ray-casting units [S1].
+This method offloads the computationally intensive geometry operations of volume rendering—specifically perspective calculations, gradient estimation, and volume data resampling—to dedicated hardware accelerators [S1]. It solves the bottleneck where software implementations consume up to 80% of computation time on these tasks [S1]. Unlike general-purpose GPU implementations that rely on texture sampling hardware, this method uses custom address generation and precalculated weight memories to perform backward mapping interpolation and gradient estimation in parallel, generating ray starting points and sample values for downstream ray-casting units [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs**
-*   **Input:** Ray starting point, ray vector (direction), volume dataset (stored in ORAMs or DRAMs), density Lookup Table (LUT).
-*   **Output:** Resampled voxel values (density), gradient components ($G_x, G_y$), and sampling point positions for the next iteration.
+*   **Input:** Ray starting point, ray vector (direction), volume dataset (stored in ORAMs or DRAMs), density Lookup Table (LUT) [S1].
+*   **Output:** Resampled voxel values (density), gradient components ($G_x, G_y$), and sampling point positions for the next iteration [S1].
 
 **Data Structures**
-*   **Weight Memory:** Size $256\text{K} \times 16$ bits. Stores precalculated interpolation weights. Addressed by three 6-bit fractional parts (one per coordinate $x, y, z$) of the resampling location.
+*   **Weight Memory:** Size $256\text{K} \times 16$ bits. Stores precalculated interpolation weights [S1]. Addressed by three 6-bit fractional parts (one per coordinate $x, y, z$) of the resampling location [S1].
 *   **Gradient Buffer:** Limits the maximal resampled dataset size to $512^3$ [S1].
 *   **Memory System:** Supports 8-neighbor access using Fast Page Mode, alternate memory bank read-out, and a 1-entry cache for previously used voxels. A controller returns 0 for addresses outside the data cube [S1].
